INSERT  INTO products (
    id,
    name,
    description,
    price
)
VALUES               (1, 'Ergonomic Mechanical Keyboard', 'A premium mechanical keyboard with hot-swappable switches, adjustable RGB lighting, and a comfortable ergonomic layout designed for long hours of typing.', 129.99),
(2, 'Stainless Steel Insulated Water Bottle', 'A double-wall vacuum insulated stainless steel bottle that keeps beverages cold for up to 24 hours or hot for up to 12 hours.', 34.95),
(3, 'Wireless Noise-Cancelling Headphones', 'Over-ear wireless headphones featuring active noise cancellation, high-quality audio, multipoint Bluetooth connectivity, and up to 30 hours of battery life.', 199.99),
(4, 'Smart Fitness Watch', 'A versatile fitness smartwatch with heart-rate monitoring, sleep tracking, GPS, workout modes, notifications, and a bright AMOLED display.', 159.50),
(5, 'Premium Chef Knife', 'A professionally balanced 8-inch Japanese-style chef knife made from high-carbon stainless steel with a sharp edge and ergonomic handle.', 89.00);

INSERT  INTO reviews (
    id,
    author,
    rating,
    content,
    createdAt,
    productId
)
VALUES              (1, 'Daniel Carter', 5, 'I have been using this keyboard for several weeks as my primary keyboard for software development, and it has been an excellent upgrade from the standard office keyboard I was using before. The mechanical switches have a satisfying amount of resistance without requiring excessive force, and the keys feel consistent across the entire board. I especially appreciate being able to customize the RGB lighting and remap several keys for shortcuts that I use frequently in my development workflow. The ergonomic design also makes a noticeable difference during long coding sessions because my wrists feel less strained at the end of the day. The build quality is solid, and there is very little flex when typing. It is not the cheapest mechanical keyboard available, but the combination of comfort, customization, and typing quality makes it well worth the price for anyone who spends many hours at a computer.', '2026-08-01 09:15:00', 1),
(2, 'Megan Foster', 4, 'This is a very capable keyboard for both work and gaming. I primarily bought it for writing and programming, and after getting used to the mechanical switches I found myself typing faster and making fewer mistakes. The hot-swappable switches are a particularly useful feature because I can experiment with different switches without replacing the entire keyboard. The stabilizers are reasonably quiet and the larger keys do not have the rattling sound I have experienced with cheaper mechanical keyboards. My only complaint is that the included wrist support could be slightly wider and softer for people with larger hands. Everything else feels thoughtfully designed, including the adjustable feet and backlighting controls. The keyboard has become one of the most frequently used pieces of equipment on my desk, and I would recommend it to anyone looking for a substantial improvement over a basic membrane keyboard.', '2026-08-04 14:30:00', 1),
(3, 'Arjun Patel', 5, 'I purchased this keyboard specifically for long programming sessions and it has exceeded my expectations. The keys have a crisp tactile response and there is enough feedback to know exactly when each key registers. I initially worried that mechanical keyboards would be too loud for my shared workspace, but these switches are much quieter than I expected. The customization software took a little time to understand, but once configured it allowed me to create useful shortcuts and lighting profiles. The keyboard also feels significantly more durable than the inexpensive keyboards I have used in the past. After several hours of continuous typing, my hands do not feel nearly as tired as they used to. The only thing I would change is adding a dedicated media control wheel, but that is a minor issue given everything else the keyboard offers.', '2026-08-08 18:45:00', 1),
(4, 'Sophie Williams', 4, 'The overall typing experience on this keyboard is excellent, particularly for someone who works from home and spends most of the day writing documents and responding to messages. The ergonomic shape took me about two days to get accustomed to, but afterward I noticed considerably less wrist discomfort. The keys are responsive and have a pleasant tactile feel without being excessively sensitive. I also like the fact that the switches can be replaced, which gives the keyboard a longer useful lifespan than many competing products. The RGB lighting is more customizable than I expected and can be kept subtle for a professional workspace. The software interface could be simpler and the included cable is somewhat stiff, but neither issue affects the core experience. It feels like a premium product that was designed around actual daily use rather than just appearance.', '2026-08-12 11:20:00', 1),
(5, 'Kevin Brooks', 5, 'As someone who works in software engineering during the day and plays games in the evening, I wanted a keyboard that could handle both activities without compromising on comfort. This one does exactly that. The switches provide excellent feedback for typing while still being responsive enough for gaming, and the construction feels sturdy enough to survive being transported between my office and home setup. I particularly enjoy the programmable keys because I use them for build commands, terminal shortcuts, and gaming macros. The lighting also looks great without being overly distracting. After using it every day for a month, there are no signs of key wobble or inconsistent switches. It is a relatively expensive keyboard, but the quality and flexibility justify the cost for me.', '2026-08-18 20:10:00', 1),
(6, 'Rachel Morgan', 5, 'This water bottle has become my everyday companion for work, commuting, and weekend hikes. The insulation is genuinely impressive. I filled it with ice water before leaving home in the morning and still had very cold water available late in the evening. The exterior does not become covered in condensation, which is especially useful when carrying it inside a laptop bag. The stainless steel construction feels durable without making the bottle unnecessarily heavy, and the lid seals tightly enough that I have had no leaks even when the bottle is stored horizontally. The opening is also large enough to add ice cubes and makes cleaning straightforward. I have tried several insulated bottles over the years, and this is one of the first that combines good temperature retention with a practical shape and comfortable drinking experience.', '2026-08-02 07:50:00', 2),
(7, 'James Anderson', 4, 'I bought this bottle primarily for long days at the office and gym, and it has performed very well. Cold drinks stay cold for most of the day, even when the bottle is left in a warm car for a couple of hours. The powder-coated exterior provides a secure grip and has not shown any scratches despite being placed in my backpack with other equipment. I also like the lid because it can be opened quickly with one hand once you get used to the mechanism. The bottle is slightly wider than I expected, so it does not fit perfectly into the cup holder of my older car, which is the only reason I am giving it four stars. Otherwise, the construction is excellent and there is no metallic taste in the water. It feels like a bottle that should last for years rather than something that will need to be replaced every season.', '2026-08-06 12:05:00', 2),
(8, 'Linda Chen', 5, 'I was looking for a reusable bottle that could handle both hot tea during my morning commute and cold water during workouts, and this one has been fantastic. I tested it with hot tea before work and it remained warm for many hours without the outside becoming uncomfortable to hold. On another day I filled it with chilled water and ice, and the contents were still very cold after an entire afternoon outdoors. The bottle has a reassuringly solid feel but is not so heavy that carrying it becomes annoying. The lid threads smoothly and creates a reliable seal. I also appreciate that the interior does not retain strong smells after washing. After several weeks of daily use, it still looks almost new. This is a simple product, but the quality of the materials and insulation make a noticeable difference compared with cheaper bottles I have owned.', '2026-08-10 16:40:00', 2),
(9, 'Michael Turner', 4, 'This bottle is particularly useful for hiking and outdoor activities because it keeps water cold for a surprisingly long time. I took it on a full-day trail during hot weather and the water was still refreshing when I reached the end of the hike. The stainless steel body feels sturdy enough for outdoor use and the lid has survived being dropped onto rocks without cracking. It fits comfortably into the side pocket of my hiking backpack, although it is a little heavier than lightweight plastic bottles. Cleaning is easy because the opening is wide enough to reach inside with a normal bottle brush. I would have liked a slightly more convenient carrying handle, but the existing one works adequately. Overall, it is a dependable bottle with excellent insulation and feels much more durable than the disposable bottles I used to carry.', '2026-08-15 10:25:00', 2),
(10, 'Emily Richardson', 5, 'I bought this bottle after becoming frustrated with plastic bottles that developed odors and stopped keeping drinks cold after a few hours. This one has been a major improvement. I usually fill it with cold water in the morning and do not need to refill it with ice throughout the workday. The stainless steel interior is easy to clean and has not picked up the taste of coffee or flavored drinks. The exterior stays dry even when the contents are extremely cold, which means I can place it beside my notebook without worrying about water rings. The lid feels robust and has never leaked in my bag. I also like the understated design because it looks appropriate in an office as well as at the gym. For the price, the combination of insulation, durability, and ease of cleaning is excellent.', '2026-08-20 08:35:00', 2),
(11, 'Chris Thompson', 5, 'These headphones have dramatically improved my experience when working in a busy environment. The active noise cancellation does a great job reducing conversations, air conditioning noise, and general background activity, allowing me to concentrate without constantly increasing the volume. The sound quality is balanced and detailed, with enough bass for music but without overwhelming vocals or podcasts. I also use them for video meetings, and the microphone has been clear enough that colleagues have not had trouble understanding me. Battery life has been excellent in my experience, easily lasting through several workdays when I remember to charge them overnight. The ear cushions are comfortable for long sessions and the headband does not put excessive pressure on my head. Multipoint Bluetooth is another feature I use constantly because I can switch between my laptop and phone without manually reconnecting each time.', '2026-08-03 13:10:00', 3),
(12, 'Jessica Adams', 4, 'I primarily purchased these headphones for frequent flights and they have made traveling much more comfortable. The noise cancellation is especially effective against the constant engine rumble, and I can listen to podcasts at a much lower volume than I normally would. Music sounds clear with a pleasant amount of detail across the midrange and high frequencies. The headphones fold reasonably well for travel and the carrying case protects them adequately in my backpack. Comfort is good for the first several hours, although the ear cushions become slightly warm during very long flights. Pairing with my phone was quick and reliable, and the connection has remained stable throughout daily use. I wish the touch controls were a little easier to operate without accidentally triggering commands, but overall these are excellent travel headphones and a substantial improvement over the inexpensive pair I previously used.', '2026-08-07 19:25:00', 3),
(13, 'Robert Garcia', 5, 'I have used these headphones for music production, casual listening, online meetings, and gaming, and they have performed consistently well across all of those activities. The sound signature is detailed enough to hear instruments clearly without making music sound overly bright or artificial. The noise cancellation is not only useful outdoors but also helps eliminate low-frequency noise from appliances and nearby traffic while working at home. I particularly appreciate the transparency mode because it lets me hear someone speaking without removing the headphones. The battery has been reliable and I rarely have to think about charging during the week. Bluetooth multipoint is also extremely convenient when moving between my desktop and phone. The build feels premium, and after daily use for more than a month there are no creaks or loose hinges. They are expensive, but the combination of audio quality and practical features makes the price reasonable.', '2026-08-11 15:55:00', 3),
(14, 'Olivia Martin', 4, 'These headphones are very comfortable for working from home and attending long video calls. The ear cups provide a good seal without feeling excessively tight, and the active noise cancellation helps create a quiet environment even when there is activity elsewhere in the house. Voice calls are clear and the microphone does a good job with normal conversation. Music has plenty of detail and podcasts sound natural, which is important because I use them for several hours every day. The physical controls are easier for me to use than touch controls on some other headphones I have tried. My main criticism is that the carrying case takes up more room than I expected, and the headphones can feel warm after several consecutive hours. Those are relatively minor drawbacks, though. Overall, these are a strong choice for productivity and everyday listening.', '2026-08-16 09:45:00', 3),
(15, 'Ethan Walker', 5, 'I bought these headphones because I needed one pair that could work equally well for commuting, gaming, and office calls. They have become my default headphones for almost everything. The noise cancellation is excellent on buses and trains, especially for low-frequency engine noise, while the transparency mode is useful when ordering coffee or talking to someone without taking the headphones off. Sound quality is rich but not overly bass-heavy, and games have a good sense of spatial detail even though these are not marketed specifically as gaming headphones. The wireless connection has been stable with both my laptop and phone, and multipoint switching works better than expected. The battery lasts long enough that I only need to charge them once or twice a week with moderate use. The price is high, but after using them daily I feel that the convenience and build quality justify the investment.', '2026-08-22 21:15:00', 3),
(16, 'Sarah Bennett', 5, 'This fitness watch has become a useful part of my daily routine because it gives me enough health and activity information without requiring me to constantly check my phone. The step tracking is consistent with my expectations, and the workout modes make it easy to record runs, cycling sessions, and strength workouts. GPS tracking has been accurate enough for my regular outdoor runs, with routes matching the paths I know well. The display is bright and readable outdoors, even in direct sunlight. Sleep tracking is also helpful for identifying patterns in my bedtime and wake-up schedule. Notifications are convenient because I can quickly see messages without taking out my phone, while the battery lasts several days with normal usage. The watch is comfortable enough to wear overnight and does not feel excessively bulky during exercise. It provides a good balance between smartwatch features and fitness-focused functionality.', '2026-08-04 06:50:00', 4),
(17, 'Thomas Wilson', 4, 'I purchased this watch mainly for running and general fitness tracking, and it has been reliable so far. GPS locks on quickly when I start an outdoor workout and the recorded distances are generally close to what I see on dedicated running apps. The heart-rate monitoring appears consistent during steady workouts, although it can take a little time to respond during sudden changes in intensity. I really like having multiple workout modes because I can track strength sessions and cycling in addition to running. The screen is one of the best features because text remains easy to read in bright sunlight. Battery life is good enough for several days, though frequent GPS use reduces it noticeably. The watch is lightweight and comfortable, and the strap has not caused irritation during long workouts. For someone looking for a practical fitness watch rather than a luxury smartwatch, this is a very solid option.', '2026-08-09 17:35:00', 4),
(18, 'Natalie Cooper', 5, 'I was initially interested in this watch because of its sleep tracking, but I have ended up using many more features than expected. The sleep reports are easy to understand and give useful information about bedtime consistency and overnight activity. During workouts, the interface makes it simple to start and stop sessions and view metrics without constantly navigating through menus. I particularly enjoy the automatic workout detection because I sometimes forget to manually start a session. Notifications are displayed clearly, and I can dismiss simple alerts directly from the watch. The AMOLED screen looks excellent and the brightness automatically adjusts well between indoor and outdoor environments. Battery life has been better than I expected, generally lasting several days before charging. The watch also looks appropriate with casual clothing rather than appearing exclusively like a piece of gym equipment, which makes it easy to wear throughout the day.', '2026-08-14 12:20:00', 4),
(19, 'Andrew Lewis', 4, 'This is my first dedicated fitness watch, so I wanted something that was straightforward rather than overloaded with complicated features. Setup was quick, and the companion app made it easy to configure notifications and activity goals. I mainly use the watch for walking, weekend cycling, and monitoring my daily steps. The GPS is useful when cycling because I can review the route afterward without carrying my phone in my hand. The heart-rate information is presented clearly and is useful for seeing how intensity changes during exercise. The battery lasts several days under normal conditions, although GPS-heavy workouts require more frequent charging. The strap is comfortable and adjustable, and the watch itself is light enough that I often forget I am wearing it. A few menu options could be easier to discover, but overall it has been an excellent introduction to fitness tracking.', '2026-08-19 08:05:00', 4),
(20, 'Grace Mitchell', 5, 'I have been using this smartwatch for both structured workouts and everyday activity tracking, and I am impressed with how well it fits into both parts of my routine. The workout tracking provides enough information to help me understand my pace and heart rate without becoming distracting. GPS performance has been particularly useful for outdoor runs, and the recorded routes have been accurate across several different neighborhoods. Sleep tracking gives me a helpful overview of my nightly habits, while the battery comfortably lasts several days for my normal usage. The AMOLED display is bright, sharp, and easy to read, and the watch responds quickly when navigating between screens. Notifications are useful but can be selectively disabled, which prevents the watch from becoming a constant source of distraction. It feels like a thoughtfully designed fitness device rather than a phone replacement, which is exactly what I wanted.', '2026-08-24 18:30:00', 4),
(21, 'Mark Evans', 5, 'This chef knife immediately felt different from the inexpensive knives I had been using for years. The blade is exceptionally sharp out of the box and makes slicing vegetables much faster and more controlled. I prepared onions, tomatoes, carrots, and boneless chicken with it, and the knife moved through each ingredient smoothly without requiring much pressure. The balance is excellent, with the weight distributed in a way that makes the knife feel stable rather than heavy. The handle is comfortable even during longer meal-preparation sessions, and the blade is narrow enough to make precise cuts while still being substantial enough for larger vegetables. I have been careful to hand wash and dry it immediately after use, and the edge has remained very sharp. This is definitely a knife that rewards proper maintenance, but for anyone who cooks regularly, the improvement in control and efficiency is significant.', '2026-08-05 18:15:00', 5),
(22, 'Hannah Scott', 4, 'I bought this knife after taking a basic cooking class where I learned how much difference a properly balanced chef knife can make. The first thing I noticed was how easily it handled repetitive chopping. The blade is sharp enough to make clean cuts through herbs and vegetables without crushing softer ingredients such as tomatoes. It also has enough length to handle larger items like cabbage and squash comfortably. The handle provides a secure grip and did not become uncomfortable during a long meal-preparation session. I have only had it for a few weeks, so I cannot comment on long-term edge retention yet, but so far it has stayed sharp with normal home cooking. The knife does require more careful cleaning and storage than my old knives, but that is expected with a higher-quality blade. It has made cooking noticeably more enjoyable and efficient.', '2026-08-09 20:40:00', 5),
(23, 'Carlos Ramirez', 5, 'As someone who cooks almost every evening, I wanted to replace my collection of mediocre knives with one dependable chef knife. This knife has become the one I reach for most often. The blade has excellent edge retention and remains sharp after preparing vegetables, herbs, meat, and fish throughout the week. The balance is especially impressive because it allows precise cuts without putting unnecessary strain on my wrist. I can perform everything from fine chopping to slicing large vegetables with confidence. The high-carbon stainless steel also gives me peace of mind because I have experienced much more surface staining with cheaper carbon-steel knives. The handle feels secure when my hands are wet, although I still make sure to dry everything immediately after washing. It is not a knife I would recommend putting into a dishwasher, but with proper care it feels like the kind of kitchen tool that could last for many years.', '2026-08-13 19:05:00', 5),
(24, 'Laura Peterson', 4, 'This knife has been a very nice addition to my home kitchen. I mostly cook vegetables, pasta dishes, stir-fries, and simple meat recipes, and the eight-inch blade has been versatile enough for nearly everything I prepare. The edge arrived extremely sharp and made thin slicing much easier than with my previous knife. The blade has enough stiffness for controlled chopping but is not so heavy that it becomes tiring. I particularly like the handle shape because it gives me a stable grip while allowing different hand positions for different cutting techniques. After several weeks of regular use, the edge is still performing well. My only hesitation is that the knife is sharp enough that beginners should take some time to learn proper cutting technique. For an experienced home cook, however, it provides excellent precision and feels considerably more professional than typical supermarket knives.', '2026-08-18 16:25:00', 5),
(25, 'Steven Hughes', 5, 'I have worked in restaurant kitchens and have used many different chef knives, so I had fairly high expectations when ordering this one for my home kitchen. It has impressed me with its combination of sharpness, balance, and comfortable handling. The blade is thin enough for precise vegetable preparation while retaining enough strength for everyday kitchen tasks. Straight out of the package, it produced very clean slices through tomatoes and onions, and after regular honing it has continued to perform well. The handle is comfortable during extended prep sessions and the knife does not feel front-heavy. I also appreciate the relatively simple design because there are fewer areas around the handle where food residue can accumulate. This is not a disposable kitchen knife and should be treated accordingly, but with hand washing, immediate drying, and occasional sharpening, I expect it to remain a reliable part of my kitchen for a very long time.', '2026-08-25 11:45:00', 5);